          "path": "_m/c/2/8/7/victoria-british-columbia-wk/craigdarroch-built-188.jpg",
          "filename": "Craigdarroch Castle May 2011.jpg",
          "caption": "Craigdarroch was built between 1887-1890 for Robert Dunsmuir, a Scottish immigrant who made his fortune from Vancouver Island coal. This legendary Victorian mansion, built on a hill overlooking the City of Victoria (Craigdarroch means \"rocky, oak place\" in Gaelic) announced to the world that Robert Dunsmuir was the richest and most important man in Western Canada.\n\nCraigdarroch Castle",
          "alt": "Craigdarroch was built between 1887-1890 for Robert Dunsmuir, a Scottish immigrant who made his fortune from Vancouver Island coal. This legendary Victorian mansion, built on a hill overlooking the City of Victoria (Craigdarroch means \"rocky, oak place\" in Gaelic) announced to the world that Robert Dunsmuir was the richest and most important man in Western Canada.\n\nCraigdarroch Castle",
